s7-6-p33 = prose (cons "For terminal heads the recursive factor is the unit type and their return/fault payloads must be related by the specified value relation. For command heads the quantification over matching continuations is dependent on the command's response type: for every response allowed by the common handler, the respective continuations are related one clock tick later. The displayed greatest relation is understood as the guarded fixed point of these clauses; the finite-prefix relation in (7.6c) is constructed **before** the guarded recursion. The established theory of bisimulation and coinduction supplies the background for such greatest relations ([57](#ref-57)); the guarded clauses and their observation conditions are the ones explicitly stated here. This prevents the unsound proof that silently diverging target code simulates a source that must return: the source has a finite return head and the target does not, and the divergence clauses also disagree. It distinguishes divergence from deadlock, rather than hiding both as absence of a head. The two-sided form is appropriate for equivalence of visible behavior; a compiler that promises only refinement uses the corresponding one-sided head inclusion with an independent progress/divergence condition. Fairness and permitted environmental responses remain premises of the selected observation model; they are not inferred from guardedness. When the chosen semantics regards internal delays themselves as observable, replace the weak-head relation by the stronger labeled relation instead." nil)
